\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Federated revocation propagation across three harbors. The cuckoo filter mechanism is unchanged from Anchor~\S  2.4 of the companion paper, but two new pieces are bolted on: (a) per-epoch roots $R_X^{(e)}$ published to a shared witness log so a third party can audit any harbor's local view, and (b) cross-witness signatures so the auditor pattern generalizes Certificate Transparency~\cite  {laurie2013ct}. The window between $t=0$ and $t=\Delta $ is the structural attacker window: bounded, named, and priced into the bond in \S  \ref {sec:fh-settlement}.}}{20}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fh-revocation}{{9}{20}{Federated revocation propagation across three harbors. The cuckoo filter mechanism is unchanged from Anchor~\S 2.4 of the companion paper, but two new pieces are bolted on: (a) per-epoch roots $R_X^{(e)}$ published to a shared witness log so a third party can audit any harbor's local view, and (b) cross-witness signatures so the auditor pattern generalizes Certificate Transparency~\cite {laurie2013ct}. The window between $t=0$ and $t=\Delta $ is the structural attacker window: bounded, named, and priced into the bond in \S \ref {sec:fh-settlement}}{figure.caption.19}{}}
\newlabel{prot:gossip}{{9.1}{20}{Federated revocation gossip}{protocol.9.1}{}}
