\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Cartel repeated-game node under the grim-trigger strategy. Each round a colluding member chooses between maintaining the floor $q_{\mathrm  {floor}}$ or undercutting it by $\varepsilon $. Detection probability $p_d$ slashes the colluder; one-shot defection takes the $\pi _D$ gain once and forfeits future $\pi _C$ stream. The sustainability inequality on the right reduces to the closed-form threshold $p_d^\star $ used in Figure~\ref {fig:cartel-folk}.}}{25}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cartel-game-inline}{{13}{25}{Cartel repeated-game node under the grim-trigger strategy. Each round a colluding member chooses between maintaining the floor $q_{\mathrm {floor}}$ or undercutting it by $\varepsilon $. Detection probability $p_d$ slashes the colluder; one-shot defection takes the $\pi _D$ gain once and forfeits future $\pi _C$ stream. The sustainability inequality on the right reduces to the closed-form threshold $p_d^\star $ used in Figure~\ref {fig:cartel-folk}}{figure.caption.25}{}}
